hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today's  question comes from one of my YouTube  viewers who asked about getting a  college degree and you wrote insane what  college degree do you think is essential  for anyone to have when certain  Enterprise if any so this is always a  tough question should I go to college or  not and if you're if you're gonna get a  college degree I would probably suggest  something in business commerce finance  just so that you understand how that  world works especially if you're coming  from a different background so if you're  a scientist or someone from the arts and  you've never done anything in business  before it could help you a lot to get a  degree in business just to understand  that world and don't be able to figure  it out through textbooks it's not the  necessarily the best learning experience  but you're gonna learn a lot more than  if you kind of stuck to the science and  arts program about how to run a business  one thing I found really helpful about  my university education so I had a  bachelor's degree from University of  Toronto  I majored in finance commerce and  economics and the education side for  running the business was not fantastic I  was already running my company at the  time and I found that learning a lot  more through hands-on experience than I  did from the textbooks in the class and  you'll find that in general you'll get  the best learning experience from  actually hands-on training and going  after what you're interested in I don't  want to suggest not going to get an  education  because it can also provide a great  back-up plan  you know not everybody is meant to be an  entrepreneur and if it doesn't work out  you want to have something that you can  fall back on and easily be able to go  out and get a job because if you don't  have a job and don't have an education  it's a lot harder to get those jobs so  it is a good backup plan and you can  also make some good connections so  you're meeting with people who might  have similar mindsets to you my first  two business partners were at the same  university that I was at  we will form our company out of the  University so meeting meeting them and  being able to start the company was  extremely helpful and that happened  through the university so you know if we  weren't all at the University would it  have happened you know maybe maybe not  but that was a useful thing as well so  you can get connections and if you ever  end up selling to big business a lot of  the guys who are in your class are gonna  go get jobs and they could be potential  leads into sales so you can make with  your company down the line so I think  the best experience you're gonna get is  the hands-on I've cut my teeth on  entrepreneurship really early with my  own little businesses and through  programs like Junior Achievement where  they make you start a business in  elementary school and that stuff was was  awesome so I still think I'm gonna get  the most from your hands-on experience  but I don't want to say don't go to  school because it's a great back-up plan  if you're not from a business background  you'll be able to get some some good  skills that'll teach you the the  fundamental basics about running the  business and you can also make some  great connections that can help you  learn more about yourself and also help  you down down the road as you do grow  your business so hopefully that helps  some tough decisions for you to make if  you guys liked the video please give it  a thumbs up below it's what makes me  want to do more things for you guys and  if you have a question about this video  or you have a different question about  your business feel free to leave it in  the comments below and I will make a  video reply for you so thank you and  we'll see you on the next episode  you
 

